put('CHAIN_COMPARISON.md','# Scientific-chain comparison\n\nScope: **independent modeling-layer replication with audited inherited preprocessing**. Two human-accepted qualifications: literal `.DS_Store` drift and Classification-B native-request provenance gap.\n\n'+table(pd.DataFrame(extra)[['stage','quantity','status','comparison_method','root_cause_or_limit']])+'''\n\n## Earliest established divergence\n\nThe first chronological feature-rule witness is KO2012-08-13 Q2, stored grid index3195. Historical native formula uses past daily-window values and current regime pseudocount without an additional current/prior guard; new native line141 returns NaN, subsequently fallback0 in scaled space. Bounded arithmetic on saved geometry yields historical-formula -0.30194697886322325, with60 finite past daily values. This is a formula witness, not an archived original native array.\n\nCOP's47 component-blocked fit-union positions start grid3525 on2012-11-01 and end2012-11-12. Original hf1m_ft16_math.py225–229 masks component values before hf20_s4_fit.fit_expanded; new features.fit_recipe150–168 uses unmasked components, then native145–146 masks final features. F21 initial COP M2 floor and hourly pseudocount are the earliest phase recipe witnesses in recipe_values.csv. Exact fit-hour membership does not imply equal per-component fitting support.\n\nOriginal hf1m_ft16_math.py180 aliases VOLUME_H to source volume; subsequent in-place component masking also changes the hourly pseudocount input. Daily volumes were constructed earlier. New V remains unmasked during pseudocount fitting. This explains the observed COP hourly but not daily pseudocount discrepancy. The complete original transitive snapshot is incompletely pinned; archived recipe differences themselves are direct evidence.\n\nBoth changes precede observed training/forecast drift. This audit does not quantify their separate causal contributions or rule out additional finite/backend drift. No corrective feature regeneration or fitting was performed.\n\n## All16 channels\n\n'''+table(pd.DataFrame(channel))+'''\n\nSeven-context M2 formulas, causal day locks,48 fixed scheduled positions, minimum counts and fallback are defined in the frozen specification and inspected implementation; original S4 witness tables corroborate historical checks. The119 scalar source witnesses and4 tensor-identity rows are earlier historical self-checks, not full S2C initial/refit tensor comparisons. Equal scalers are not proof of equal full features.\n\nSource/clock/label rules agree by direct labels/roles and inspected definition:09:30 genuine open, nonopening preceding-minute close,240 scheduled minutes, terminal stub for labels only,48 completed full-hour positions, same fixed20 stocks. All20 role indices exactly equal. All candidate return/mask comparisons include weekend/DST/half-day periods; these are direct value agreement, not independent proof of historical calendar announcement/vintage.\n\nNo new positive evidence of protected data, old-helper use during Phase2, target/role contamination or inference auxiliary-label input was observed. This is bounded available-evidence review, not proof such access was impossible. F09 and starred issuance mismatch persist.\n''')
put('FORECAST_PARITY.md','# Forecast parity\n\nOriginal per-row C-A predictions ARE archived. All four OOS files (80260 rows) and calibration files (18980 rows) have exact unique key coverage, fixed20 stock axis and matching timestamp/category metadata; labels and weights match at required precision. Full candidate signedR and auxiliary targets additionally match the bound S4 archive exactly.\n\n'+table(fullfr)+'''\n\nDifferences are new minus original; correlation is descriptive, not parity. The diagnostic float32 tier is fixed at atol1e-6+rtol1e-5*abs(original). Many rows exceed it. No tolerance was widened. Per-stock/slot/category/p95/p99 summaries and p95/p99 error statistics are in FORECAST_PARITY.csv.\n\nNo original or independent RAW/C3 prediction is clamped to zero and no predicted ties are present. Nonetheless390 of762470 within-origin unordered pairs change order:53,109,82,146 in2021–24;368 origins are affected. The same pairs flip for Mhat/RAW/C3 because decoding is monotone per origin. Small near-order margins explain how nearly equal scalar MSE coexists with IC changes; this is not a tie/clamp bug. Pair witnesses include original margins in comparisons/pair_order_disagreements.csv.\n\nMax C3 differences concentrate in2024; the largest stock-group maximum is SBUX, followed by BA and TSLA. Shared training can propagate stock-local feature changes to all names, so this pattern does not isolate a cause. First chronological joined-key differences are in first_difference_witnesses.csv.\n\nOld per-row signed-head outputs are absent from the C-A forecast schema; only signed aggregate diagnostics can be compared. No original forecasts were generated.\n''')
put('ORIGINAL_VS_INDEPENDENT_METRICS.md','# Original versus independent metrics\n\nAll available C-A RAW/C3 full and conditional annual/EQ scalar/rank results, slot/calendar/tail values, event retrieval and annual signed diagnostics are compared at saved precision in the CSV.3912 matched numeric cells were compared; absent main-stock/conditional-rank/signed-EQ cells are explicitly NOT_COMPARABLE/NOT_ARCHIVED, not zero. Old NORMAL maps to REGULAR, tail_ALL/PREFIX95 to ALL:p95:event, and next_open_to_exit to post; these are explicit schema mappings. C0-deciles remain out of scope.\n\n## Primary C3 screen\n\n'+table(headline)+'''\n\nAll15 primary tests pass the predeclared screening bounds: relative MSE/MAE<=1e-4, absolute IC<=.0005. The broader method is not numerically equivalent because feature procedures/recipes differ and many per-row predictions exceed the diagnostic tier. Labels' annual/EQ observed means agree.\n\nIndependent arithmetic checks precede interpretation: compare.py recomputes both archives' full/category scalar and rank results; deep_checks.py separately uses Python fsum over stock→origin→session means and hand average-rank formulas; all_metric_audit.py recomputes all five Phase2 tables including conditional scopes, events, signed diagnostics and clamping. Maximum full-table difference2.22e-15, no undefined-value mismatch. Checks use round-trip CSV parsing and explicit full-key alignment; no positional score join.\n\nConditional scalar estimates retain original annual cell weights; conditional ranks regroup origins/sessions. Equal-year estimates average annual values; primary ratio uses mean predicted/mean observed. Tail cutoffs come from frozen refit records and are checked against exact integer-mass oracles, never estimated from OOS. No comparator fits or paired comparator inference were performed. Similar S2C outputs do not validate the original small improvement over CLOCK/classical baselines. Repeatedly inspected exploratory years and overlapping targets preclude an untouched-holdout or IID significance interpretation.\n''')
put('EXISTING_DEVIATIONS_AND_LIMITATIONS.md','''# Existing deviations and limitations — preserved\n\nThe following remain separate from P3N001–P3N012. No old FAIL or STOP was rewritten.\n\n- **Accepted metadata qualification:** only literal phase2/.DS_Store can differ. Original expected, first observed, continuation observed and current observed hashes are retained in prior reports and the new gate.232 substantive payloads match; not233-file byte parity. No repair/restore/chmod.\n- **Accepted Classification B:**39 receipts have zero admitted_data_request despite final boundary.data_path insertion. Preparation-time body/module identity and exhaustive native reads are unknown.348 identities,2272 saved aggregation assertions and geometry/consumption evidence support bounded lineage, not complete native-read logging. Postrun path aggregation overstated coverage. No invented events or retroactive PASS.\n- **D01 / starred issuance mismatch:** nominal t target versus assumed t+2 availability;09:30 reference from minute-open bar. Preserved, not live-tradable proof.\n- **D02–D05:** independent prefit coding corrections, not historical defects/neural retries. Original correction log retained. No new fit was run here.\n- **D06:** original final signed-report run failed on a pandas read-only boolean view after8 fitting phases. Original failure, executed evaluator snapshot, one-line.copy diff, source transition,80 unchanged fitted files,4 checkpoint/8 role reload receipts and5 byte-identical replay pairs verified. One report-only recovery, zero neural/calibration/threshold retries. No claim of an error-free original report run.\n- **D07:** synthetic600 equal-mass weighted-left boundary FAIL remains. Separate integer-weight arithmetic on saved role targets reproduces all8 phase scales and8 actual tail thresholds exactly; actual threshold membership is unchanged. The generalized edge is not patched or relabeled PASS.\n- **D08:** PROCEDURAL_ORDER_DIFFERENCE_WITH_SUPPORTED_DEPENDENCY_EQUIVALENCE. run_experiment.py83–95 computes raw OOS forwards before C3; predict_heads uses eval/inference mode, onlyX/CLOCK, no optimizer or dropout draws. fit_c3 consumes calibration table only, decoded OOS follows coefficient freezing. Saved coefficient arithmetic agrees. No literal-order PASS and no unrecorded live execution claim.\n\nInherited minute cleaning, corporate actions/quarantines/hourly aggregation, survivor-name economic history, fixed retrospective source vintage, F09 future-complete20 selection, calendar announcement/receipt proxies, overlapping targets, repeated development-year inspection and incomplete historical binaries remain limitations. The study predicts price-only absolute endpoint magnitudes; no execution costs/portfolio/trading P&L is evaluated.\n''')
